"t":"Syria has no plans to send troops to Yemen — The National","u":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxQcVhvVHZXZ3IweTZVTEphaFRZUlk3TWUwc3RDb0FPMGROck5Tb2xrMDQxcF9QS3JTMHk5U2pwZmpqRGFjaDF4QXhSWFctQlVHNUZNcFNkQm5ULXM5TFQzM2ltRFhtS1VFMDZ4QjNHZkJaUUU0V01TendfZHdrb1VKYnVNQUx2c0FvUHZQN2F1ZFFoWUItSXNrVGlLeEdBOXJJd1F0bXA1UzBoUlI2RFdhU09B?oc=5","p":"UA.NEWS","d":"2026-11-10T01:09:45Z","o":false,"dup":false}],"related":[],"revisions":[],"entities":[{"name":"Syria","kind":"place","mentions":11},{"name":"Yemen","kind":"place","mentions":10},{"name":"Saudi Arabia","kind":"place","mentions":5},{"name":"Houthis","kind":"person","mentions":4},{"name":"Damascus","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"Saudi","kind":"group","mentions":1},{"name":"Syrian","kind":"group","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":null,"context":{"background":[{"title":"Syrian civil war","extract":"The Syrian civil war was an armed conflict that began with the Syrian revolution in March 2011, when popular discontent with the Ba'athist regime ruled by Bashar al-Assad triggered large-scale protests and pro-democracy rallies across Syria, as part of the wider Arab Spring. The Assad regime responded to the protests with lethal force, which led to a series of defections, the emergence of armed opposition groups, and the civilian uprising descending into a civil war. The war lasted almost 14 years and culminated in the fall of the Assad regime in December 2024. Many sources regard this as the end of the civil war even though clashes have continued into 2026.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrian_civil_war","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"title":"Yemeni civil war (2014–present)","extract":"The Yemeni civil war is an ongoing multilateral civil war that began in late 2014 mainly between the Rashad al-Alimi-led Presidential Leadership Council and the Mahdi al-Mashat-led Supreme Political Council, along with their respective supporters and allies. Both sides claim to constitute the official government of Yemen while the Presidential Leadership Council is recognized by the United Nations as the official government.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yemeni_civil_war_(2014%E2%80%93present)","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"Yemen","extract":"Yemen, officially the Republic of Yemen, is a country in West Asia. Located in southern Arabia, the country includes the Socotra Archipelago and borders Saudi Arabia to the north, Oman to the northeast, the Arabian Sea to the east, the Gulf of Aden to the south, and the Red Sea to the west. It also shares maritime borders with Djibouti, Eritrea, and Somalia across the Horn of Africa. Covering 455,503 square kilometres (175,871 sq mi), with a coastline of approximately 2,000 kilometres (1,200 mi), Yemen is the second-largest country on the Arabian Peninsula by both area and population. Sanaa is its constitutional capital and largest city. Yemen's population is estimated at 34.7 million, predominantly Muslim Arabs.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yemen","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"YE"},{"title":"Syria","extract":"Syria, officially the Syrian Arab Republic, is a country in West Asia located in the Eastern Mediterranean and the Levant. It borders the Mediterranean Sea to the west, Turkey to the north and northwest, Iraq to the east and southeast, Jordan to the south, and Israel and Lebanon to the southwest. It is a republic under a provisional government and comprises 14 governorates. Damascus is Syria's capital and largest city. With a population of 26 million across an area of 185,180 square kilometres (71,500 sq mi), it is the 56th-most populous and 87th-largest country.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syria","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"SY"}],"arc":{"reports":111,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T19:12:00Z","first_title":"Saudi Arabia Closes Riyadh Airport After Dozens Hurt in Houthi Missile Attack","first_url":"h